  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening climate action in Colombia - Phase II Amazonas</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to: Design an adaptation plan that enables indigenous communities to generate climate-resilient community processes. Two plans have been developed in the Colombian Paramo in the year 2021-2022 (ancestral adaptation plan in Siachoque, Boyac&#xE1;). This project will develop this process in Amazonas. The effects of climate change on women and young people in the communities of the Amazon region will be made known through the documentary piece. The socio-environmental projects carried out by Climalab will be made visible on the regional FOSPA stage, as a way of showing the environmental impact that the Colombian Amazon region is experiencing. At the same time, Climalab&apos;s youth climate action platform will be implemented as a scenario for the consolidation of national youth climate actions.</narrative>
  </description>
